<title>USA: Projectavision says suit won't stop TV shipments.</title>
<headline>Projectavision says suit won't stop TV shipments.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Projectavision Inc said Thursday that producion of the company's new Digital Home Theater is proceeding on schedule.</p>
<p>The company stated there is no claim in a pending lawsuit that would prevent it from manufacturing, selling or shipping its Digital Home Theater televisions.  </p>
<p>Those televisions are scheduled to begin selling in New York area stores within weeks, said the compnay.</p>
<p>The principal in the lawsuit, Euguene Dolgoff, is a founder of Projectavision no longer with the company. He could not be immediately reached for comment.</p>
</text>
